From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:38:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] search_engines: make DuckDuckGo the fallback default search
 engine

GetPrepopulatedFallbackSearch() returns DuckDuckGo, looked up in the
regional list first and in the full list for the regions whose list
lacks it, instead of Google. The fallback is the default search engine
of every profile where neither the user nor policy has chosen one. With
Google as the default, the New Tab page loads Google's logo, bar and
promos, and the bar's scripts log to play.google.com.

Why: the fallback engine id is a constant inside this function; the
search_provider_overrides pref could change it only by replacing every
region's engine list.
Upstream: not upstreamable: product-specific default

Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc b/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc
index ac35ec257779f4ecaa56424b5b5de1dbf6719d3c..bc5c7d27315db29835ca332ab0d62bbb34d23eb7 100644
--- a/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc
+++ b/components/search_engines/template_url_prepopulate_data.cc
@@ -278,6 +278,14 @@ std::unique_ptr<TemplateURLData> GetPrepopulatedFallbackSearch(
     PrefService& prefs,
     const std::vector<raw_ptr<const PrepopulatedEngine>>&
         regional_prepopulated_engines) {
+  // DuckDuckGo is the default in every region. Most regional lists include it;
+  // elsewhere it comes from the full list, and TemplateURLService adds a
+  // fallback engine that the regional list lacks.
+  if (std::unique_ptr<TemplateURLData> engine =
+          GetPrepopulatedEngineFromFullList(
+              prefs, regional_prepopulated_engines, duckduckgo.id)) {
+    return engine;
+  }
   return FindPrepopulatedEngineInternal(prefs, regional_prepopulated_engines,
                                         google.id,
                                         /*use_first_as_fallback=*/true);
